        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "EO 12921 (signed 1994-06-13; 59 FR 30667) was read in full in the held Federal Register text jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_12921.txt. It raises the membership limit of the United States Advisory Council on the National Information Infrastructure in section 1(a) of Executive Order 12864 from 30 to 37. The dossier evidence ACT:EO:12921>EO:13062 was re-read against the held EO 13062 text: section 3(d) revokes EO 12864 as amended by EO 12890, EO 12921 and EO 12970, and section 7 gives the express effective date 1997-09-30. EO 12970 (1995-09-14) amends section 4(b) of EO 12864 to run until 1996-06-01 unless otherwise extended. Machine searches read: U.S. Code 0 hits, eCFR 0 hits, Federal Register catalog 2 hits. Under the owner rulings of 2026-10-21 and 2026-10-28 the end is the order that names EO 12921, with the parent’s scheduled sunset disclosed.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"Candidates tested for an earlier end: EO 12864 section 4(b), as amended by EO 12970, keeps the Council in existence until 1996-06-01 unless otherwise extended, which is an earlier scheduled sunset of the parent Council. No held source shows whether it was extended or when the Council ceased, and EO 13062 recites that its listed committees have terminated and completed their work without a date. This candidate is in the parent’s section and not a term of EO 12921; it is disclosed and not adopted. No other held order names EO 12921.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The order has one operative command, the membership change; the recital of purpose is not a separate command.\",\"savings_check\":\"Read for savings: EO 13062 section 3 has no savings language. Accrued effect: appointments of members under the raised limit.\",\"scope_check\":\"The whole order is one amendment of section 1(a) of EO 12864 (30 to 37 members). EO 12970 changes section 4(b) of the parent and not this clause. EO 13062 revokes the whole parent as amended by this order.\"}",
